  "content": {
    "id": "p14-q17-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "17",
    "prompt": "A forgetful person lets a personal loan balance grow from $\\$800$ to $\\$1440$ with a compound interest rate of 12.5% p.a. Approximately how many years did the person forget about the loan?\nHint: set up the compound interest equation and use trial and error to estimate n. Refine your trials around the target, then round the estimated time as requested.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "Approximately 5 years; $800(1.125)^5\\approx\\$1441.63$.",
      "worked": "$$1440=800(1.125)^n$$\nGuess and check whole-number values of $n$:\n$$\\begin{align*}FV(4) &= 800(1.125)^4 \\approx \\$1281.45\\\\FV(5) &= 800(1.125)^5 \\approx \\$1441.63\\\\FV(6) &= 800(1.125)^6 \\approx \\$1621.83\\end{align*}$$\nThe balance after 5 years is closest to $\\$1440$, so approximately 5 years.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 40
  },
